# docportal starts up: main.startup runs these steps in order, and main hands
# the address and the handler, the previews handler behind the sign-in
# middleware with an issuer, to the HTTP server. The builder, the build
# method of main.builder, runs boxes 7, 5, 13, 6 and 3 again for each new
# snapshot, and the preview builder, its buildPreview method, runs boxes 7,
# 5, 13 and 3 for the snapshot of each preview folder, without the chat. The
# previews handler passes box 14 on its way to box 12.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number docs/flow.dfd -o flow.svg

{Operator}
> arguments, environment
[1. Read the configuration
 from the flags and the environment
 (main.parseConfig)]
> configuration
[2. Open the documentation source: the directory of the configuration file, or the bucket folder that -root names, without its previews location
 so that every read of the directory stays inside it, and box 8 loads the published documentation alone
 (main.openSource)]
    > documentation root name
    < directory handle
    <Documentation root>
    > bucket folder URL
    < bucket
    <Bucket folder>
> source
[8. Load the source's snapshot: list it and read the listing's files into memory
 so that every request reads one version of the documentation
 (source.Load)]
    > keys
    < listing, files
    <Bucket folder>
> documentation root handle, configuration file path
[7. Read the portals from the configuration file
 into the portal configuration
 (portal.ReadConfig)]
    > configuration file path
    < configuration file
    <Documentation root>
> portal configuration, Try It setting
[5. Add the Try It setting to the portal configuration
 so that the viewer page shows or hides the Try It console
 (main.setTryIt)]
> portal configuration, issuer
[13. Add the account hook of the sign-in to the portal configuration, with an issuer
 so that every page ends with the reader's name and a sign-out link
 (main.addAccount)]
> portal configuration, chat model, chat, issuer
[6. Add the chat to the portal configuration, if a chat model is named, with the chat kept from the last snapshot, and with an issuer the reader hook of the sign-in
 so that the portal handler serves a chat page in every portal, the chat keeps its conversations, and a signed-in reader's questions count against one limit
 (main.addChat)]
    > chat
    < chat
    |Chat|
> portal configuration
[3. Build the portal handler, which answers each request with the pages of the portals and sections visible to its reader, or refuse portals that openPortals refuses, or missing Elements assets
 (portal.New)]
> source, listing, portal handler, refresh interval, builder
[9. Wrap the portal handler in the reloader, which checks the source every refresh interval and, for each settled change, builds the new snapshot's handler with the builder and swaps it in
 so that the documentation follows the bucket folder without a restart
 (source.NewReloader)]
> configuration, preview builder
[10. Open the previews location named by -previews, if any, into the previews configuration
 so that the previews handler opens the portal handler of each preview folder, loaded at the folder's first request with the preview builder
 (main.openPreviews)]
    > bucket folder URL
    < bucket
    <Bucket folder>
> reloader, previews configuration
[11. Wrap the reloader in the previews handler, which switches readers in and out of previews at /previews/ and sends each request to the portal handler of the reader's preview or to the reloader
 (portal.WithPreviews, portal.previews.ServeHTTP)]
> sign-in settings
[14. Make the sign-in configuration of the sign-in settings: none without an issuer, and with one a random session key, with a notice in the log, when the settings hold none
 (main.signInConfigOf)]
    > notice
    <Log>
> sign-in configuration, previews handler
[12. Wrap the previews handler in the sign-in middleware, with an issuer: the middleware signs each reader in through the identity provider and puts the reader's identity into each request's context
 (main.signIn)]
> address, handler
{HTTP server}

# type: arguments = []string
# type: environment = func(string) string
# type: configuration = main.config
# type: documentation root name = string
# type: directory handle = *os.Root
# type: bucket folder URL = string
# type: bucket = *gocloud.dev/blob.Bucket
# type: source = source.Source
# type: keys = []string
# type: listing = source.Listing
# type: files = [][]byte
# type: documentation root handle = io/fs.FS
# type: configuration file path = string
# type: configuration file = []byte
# type: Try It setting = bool
# type: chat model = string
# type: chat = *chat.Chat
# type: portal configuration = portal.Config
# type: portal handler = net/http.Handler
# type: refresh interval = time.Duration
# type: builder = func(io/fs.FS) (net/http.Handler, error)
# type: preview builder = func(io/fs.FS) (net/http.Handler, error)
# type: previews configuration = portal.PreviewsConfig
# type: issuer = string
# type: sign-in settings = main.signInConfig
# type: notice = string
# type: sign-in configuration = signin.Config
# type: address = string
# type: reloader = net/http.Handler
# type: previews handler = net/http.Handler
# type: handler = net/http.Handler
